Design a 16-bit wide adder with a 1-bit carry output, capable of producing a 17-bit sum. The module computes the sum of two 16-bit input values, `a` and `b`, and also generates a derived carry value based on the most significant bit of the initial sum. The output `sum` reflects the combined result of the addition, including the carry bit, thus allowing for detection of overflow in the addition operation.
module top_module(
    input [15:0] a,
    input [15:0] b,
    output reg [16:0] sum  // Changed output to reg type
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [15:0] a,
    input [15:0] b,
    output reg [16:0] sum  // Changed output to reg type
);reg [16:0] carry;
reg [16:0] temp_sum;

always @(*) begin
    temp_sum = a + b;
    carry = {temp_sum[16], temp_sum[15]};
    sum = temp_sum + (carry << 1);
end

endmodule

