description:
Design a 24-to-5 binary priority encoder. The module takes a 24-bit input signal where each bit represents a unique input. The output will be a 5-bit value that indicates the position of the highest-priority active input (the rightmost bit with a value of 1), with lower priority assigned to bits with higher indices. If no inputs are active, the output defaults to an arbitrary value of 23.
